          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"category\":\"persistent_LVDS_signal_loss\",\"cause\":\"unknown; suspected loss of the LVDS connection or upstream signal on pin16, affecting detector channels 32/33. Intentional suppression or a readout/configuration issue remains possible.\",\"action\":\"First verify whether channels 32/33 are expected to be active and whether their masking is intentional. Compare exposure-normalized raw digitizer occupancy with LVDS pin16 counts and inspect event-level channel presence. If the signal should be present and remains absent, stop the run and inspect/reseat the pin16 LVDS connections, jumper wires, and corresponding digitizer/trigger-board connectors; then start a new run and verify pin counts and channel presence. If reseating does not restore the signal, swap/test the cable or input to localize the failed component.\",\"confidence\":0.88,\"supporting_historical_runs\":[1747,2068,2071,2126],\"reasoning_summary\":\"OBSERVED: LVDS pin16 is persistently zero/abnormally low and maps specifically to channels 32/33, which are repeatedly reported missing and also show waveform-feature anomalies. Other signal pins have similar nonzero medians, while the total trigger rate remains stable. Channels 32/33 are among masked physical pins. INFERRED: the strongest diagnosis is a localized absent LVDS/upstream signal rather than a detector-wide trigger-rate failure. Historical runs 1747, 2068, 2071, and 2126 provide partial analogies involving faulty or intermittent LVDS connections, but no exact historical match is present. CONTRADICTING/AMBIGUOUS: stable trigger rate and masking could make the absence intentional or reduce its trigger impact; the end-of-run count transitions may reflect short exposure. UNKNOWN: raw digitizer occupancy, board matching, queue state, synchronization, within-run configuration, and connector status are unavailable and are needed to distinguish cabling, electronics, configuration, and upstream detector causes.\"}"
        }
      ],
      "phase": "final_answer",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
